          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#statements"} Statements
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_entries"} Related entries
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesInEquivariantCohomology"} In equivariant cohomology
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Adams conjecture
            is a statement about triviality of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+fibrations"} spherical fibrations
            associated to certain formal differences of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            classes) via the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-homomorphism
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Adams63"} Adams 63, conjecture 1.2
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+CW-complex"} finite CW-complex
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Adams63"} Adams 63, theorem 1.4
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Quillen71"} Quillen 71
          %p
            The Adams conjecture/Adams-Quillen theorem serves a central role in the identification of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image+of+the+J-homomorphism"} image of the J-homomorphism
          %h2#statements Statements
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of) a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi B
                  %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow B O
            classifying a real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+fibration"} spherical fibration
            is classified by the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi V
                  %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi J
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  J(V)
                  \\;\colon\;
                  X \stackrel{V}{\longrightarrow} B O \stackrel{J}{\longrightarrow} B GL_1(\mathbb{S})
          %p
            with the delooped
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-homomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+fibrations"} spherical fibrations
          %p
            Now for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
            on some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and for non-vanishing
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Adams"} John Adams
            observed that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+fibration"} spherical fibration
            associated with the difference
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                  %mo −
                  %mi L
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi K
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{\otimes k} - L \in K O(X)
            has the property that some
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \in \mathbb{N}
            for which
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi k
                          %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  J\left(
                  \\oplus^{k^N} (L^{\otimes k} - L)
                  \\right)
                  \= 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            Noticing that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \mapsto L^{\otimes^k} = \Psi^k(L)
            is the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+operation"} Adams operation
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            applied to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Adams"} John Adams
            then conjectured that the above is true for all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            in the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi k
                          %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ψ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  J\left(
                  \\oplus^{k^N} (\Psi^k(V) - V)
                  \\right)
                  \= 0
                  \\,.
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-homomorphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schur+index"} Schur index
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The conjecture originates in:
          %ul
            %li#Adams63
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Adams"}> John Adams
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  On the groups
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(X)
                  I: Topology
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dai+Tamaki"}> Dai Tamaki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akira+Kono"} Akira Kono
              = succeed "," do
                %em Generalized Cohomology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/mmono-230"} ISBN: 978-0-8218-3514-2
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akhil+Mathew"}> Akhil Mathew
                ,
                %em The Adams conjecture I
                (
                %a{:href => "http://amathew.wordpress.com/2013/01/23/the-adams-conjecture-i/"}> web
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                (notes by
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akhil+Mathew"} Akhil Mathew
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spectra and stable homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.uchicago.edu/~amathew/256y.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HopkinsMathewStableHomotopyTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            of the Adams conjecture is originally due to
          %ul
            %li#Quillen71
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Adams conjecture
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math1.unice.fr/~cazanave/Gdt/ImJ/Quillen.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The proof using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"}> Dennis Sullivan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Genetics of homotopy theory and the Adams conjecture
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1970841"} JSTOR
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math1.unice.fr/~cazanave/Gdt/ImJ/Sullivan.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Yet another proof via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Becker-Gottlieb+transfer"} Becker-Gottlieb transfer
            is due to
          %ul
            %li
              J. Becker, D. Gottlieb,
              %em The transfer map and fiber bundles
              Topology , 14 (1975)
          %h3#ReferencesInEquivariantCohomology In equivariant cohomology
          %p
            The generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"}> equivariant K-theory
            ) is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"}> Tammo tom Dieck
                , theorem 11.3.8 in
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Transformation+Groups+and+Representation+Theory"} Transformation Groups and Representation Theory
                Lecture Notes in Mathematics 766 Springer 1979
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zbigniew+Fiedorowicz"}> Zbigniew Fiedorowicz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henning+Hauschild"} Henning Hauschild
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                = succeed "," do
